Wine ntdll: keep the \\.\ prefix when the current directory is a device path such as \\.\GLOBALROOT\Device\HarddiskVolume1\dir. RtlSetCurrentDirectory_U stripped \??\ from the NT name and stored GLOBALROOT\Device\..., a relative path, so FenixSystem 3.0, which the runner starts in such a folder, resolved transitionAltitudes.xml and its engine model to doubled paths and stopped.
Applies to wine-cachyos with: patch -p1 --forward --fuzz=0 -i <this file>

--- a/dlls/ntdll/path.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/path.c
@@ -1040,6 +1040,13 @@
         size -= 2;
         *ptr = '\\';
     }
+    else if (size < 2 || ptr[1] != ':')
+    {
+        ptr -= 4;
+        size += 4;
+        ptr[1] = '\\';
+        ptr[2] = '.';
+    }
 
     RtlAcquirePebLock();
     if (0 && NtCurrentTeb()->Tib.SubSystemTib)  /* FIXME: hack */
